    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "see, even that \"alternative approach\" sounds like a way for them to just pay a fine and keep doing whatever they want. it feels like every time people talk about \"regulatory frameworks,\" it just turns into more lobbying from the giants to keep things exactly as they are. if you had to pick, isn't it true that the only way to actually prevent a total monopoly on data and attention is through aggressive, structural breakups?",
