      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The revolving door effect in regulatory agencies and the revolving lobbying industry create a self-interested system that may prioritize smooth disruptions over meaningful change. Given the obstacles to meaningful reform, an aggressive, structural breakup of dominant tech companies, such as a Section 2 antitrust case, might be a necessary step towards creating a truly level playing field for aspiring competitors.",
      "source": "target",
